  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amentum Services has $2.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Amentum Services received 346 awards, with an average award size of $7.3M. Amentum Services obligations are down 28.8% year over year. Amentum Services collected $1.6B from the Department of Defense and $749M from the Department of Homeland Security in FY2026 to date. Amentum Services also recorded obligations from the Department of the Treasury ($81.9M), the General Services Administration ($77.8M), and other agencies including the Department of State ($29.7M) and NASA ($24.4M). Amentum Services largest markets by NAICS in FY2026 to date are Other Support Activities for Air Transportation ($894M) and Security Guards and Patrol Services ($507M). Amentum Services also had significant obligations in Engineering Services ($279M), Facilities Support Services ($223M), and Computer Facilities Management Services ($125M). Historical obligations show Amentum Services at $1.4B in FY21, $1.6B in FY22, $2.5B in FY23, $3.8B in FY24, $3.5B in FY25, and $2.5B in FY26.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Amentum Services' biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest customer, with $1.6B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $749M. The Department of the Treasury ($81.9M) and the General Services Administration ($77.8M) are next, with smaller obligations from the Department of State ($29.7M) and NASA ($24.4M)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets does Amentum Services serve for the federal government?",
        "body": "Other Support Activities for Air Transportation is the largest market at $894M in FY2026 to date. Security Guards and Patrol Services is the second-largest market at $507M, followed by Engineering Services ($279M) and Facilities Support Services ($223M). Computer Facilities Management Services ($125M) and General Warehousing and Storage ($126M) are also notable markets."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Amentum Services make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Amentum Services has received $2.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Amentum Services received 346 awards this fiscal year to date and the average award size was $7.3M. Amentum Services obligations are down 28.8% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Amentum Services?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense, the Department of Homeland Security, the Department of the Treasury, and the General Services Administration are among Amentum Services' top buyers. The Department of Defense obligated $1.6B and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $749M in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury obligated $81.9M and the General Services Administration obligated $77.8M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Amentum Services sell to the government?",
      "a": "Amentum Services sells air support, security, engineering, facilities, and IT services to the government. Other Support Activities for Air Transportation accounted for $894M and Security Guards and Patrol Services accounted for $507M in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services ($279M), Facilities Support Services ($223M), Computer Facilities Management Services ($125M), and General Warehousing and Storage ($126M) are other top markets."
    },
